---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import GlossaryAutoLink from '../../components/GlossaryAutoLink.astro';
import BlogArticleExtras from '../../components/BlogArticleExtras.astro';
import CTASection from '../../components/CTASection.astro';
import GuideComparisons from '../../components/GuideComparisons.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';

const articleJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BlogPosting",
  "headline": "OpenAI Moderation vs Azure vs Llama Guard: A 2026 Comparison",
  "description": "A fair comparison of the main AI moderation providers on performance, pricing and language coverage.",
  "datePublished": "2026-06-10",
  "dateModified": "2026-09-04",
  "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "OpenModeration", "url": "https://www.openmoderation.com" },
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "OpenModeration",
    "logo": { "@type": "ImageObject", "url": "https://www.openmoderation.com/logo.svg" }
  },
  "image": "https://www.openmoderation.com/og-image.jpg",
  "mainEntityOfPage": { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": "https://www.openmoderation.com/blog/openai-vs-azure-vs-llama-guard-comparison" }
};
---

<BaseLayout title="OpenAI Moderation vs Azure vs Llama Guard: A 2026 Comparison" description="Compare OpenAI Moderation API, Azure AI Content Safety and Llama Guard side by side: performance, pricing, language support and when to use each." jsonLd={articleJsonLd}>
<Breadcrumb items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Blog", href: "/blog" }, { label: "Provider Comparison" }]} />
  <GlossaryAutoLink>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="mb-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 text-sm text-surface-400">
        <time datetime="2026-06-10">June 10, 2026</time>
        <span>&middot;</span>
        <span>Updated September 4, 2026</span>
        <span>&middot;</span>
        <span>8 min read</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-surface-900 sm:text-4xl">OpenAI Moderation vs Azure vs Llama Guard: A 2026 Comparison</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-surface max-w-none text-surface-600">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
        Choosing a moderation provider is one of the bigger decisions for any platform that
        hosts user-generated content. Comparing them is hard, because each one has its own API,
        its own categories, its own pricing and its own language coverage.
      </p>
      <p>
        In this post, we compare the three most common options: <strong>OpenAI Moderation API</strong>,
        <strong>Azure AI Content Safety</strong>, and <strong>Meta's Llama Guard</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900">OpenAI Moderation API</h2>
      <p>
        OpenAI's Moderation API is the most widely used AI moderation service. It sits inside
        the OpenAI platform and needs no extra infrastructure.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Strengths:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Excellent accuracy on English, consistently the best of the three</li>
        <li>Detailed categories, including hate, harassment, sexual, violence, self-harm and illicit</li>
        <li>Simple API: you send text and get scores back</li>
        <li>Low latency, typically 200-300ms</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Limitations:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Vendor lock-in: switching means rewriting your integration</li>
        <li>32K character input limit</li>
        <li>Uneven outside English: good for major European languages, weaker for others</li>
        <li>No image or video moderation</li>
        <li>Pricing: free (OpenAI states that the moderation endpoint is free to use)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900">Azure AI Content Safety</h2>
      <p>
        Microsoft's Azure AI Content Safety is the usual enterprise pick. It is part of Azure
        and offers strong compliance features and support for text and images.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Strengths:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Enterprise compliance certifications: SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA</li>
        <li>Supports both text and image moderation</li>
        <li>Custom severity thresholds and blocklists</li>
        <li>Good integration with other Azure services</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Limitations:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Requires an Azure subscription, which can stop smaller teams</li>
        <li>Vendor lock-in to Microsoft</li>
        <li>More complex authentication and API structure</li>
        <li>Pricing: billed per 1,000 text records (one record is up to 1,000 characters), with a free tier of 5,000 records a month; the paid rate depends on your Azure region</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900">Llama Guard (HuggingFace)</h2>
      <p>
        Meta's Llama Guard is a safety classification model built for this job and available on HuggingFace.
        It's open source, free to use, and can run on your own hardware.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Strengths:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Free, with no API costs and no usage limits</li>
        <li>Runs locally, so no data leaves your infrastructure</li>
        <li>Open source, so you can audit and customize it</li>
        <li>No vendor lock-in</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Limitations:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Requires GPU hardware for reasonable latency</li>
        <li>1-2 second latency on GPU, much slower on CPU</li>
        <li>English-only in practice</li>
        <li>No managed API: you host it yourself or use the HF Inference API</li>
        <li>Fewer categories than OpenAI</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900">Side-by-side comparison</h2>
      <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-surface-200">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-surface-100">
              <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold text-surface-900">Criterion</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold text-surface-900">OpenAI</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold text-surface-900">Azure</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold text-surface-900">Llama Guard</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-surface-200">
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">English accuracy</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-accent-600">Best</td><td class="px-4 py-3">Good</td><td class="px-4 py-3">Good</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Non-English support</td><td class="px-4 py-3">Good (major langs)</td><td class="px-4 py-3">Good</td><td class="px-4 py-3">Limited</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Latency</td><td class="px-4 py-3">~250ms</td><td class="px-4 py-3">~300ms</td><td class="px-4 py-3">~1.5s (GPU)</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Pricing</td><td class="px-4 py-3">Free</td><td class="px-4 py-3">Per 1K text records, varies by region</td><td class="px-4 py-3">$0 (self-hosted)</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Self-hostable</td><td class="px-4 py-3">No</td><td class="px-4 py-3">No</td><td class="px-4 py-3">Yes</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Open source</td><td class="px-4 py-3">No</td><td class="px-4 py-3">No</td><td class="px-4 py-3">Yes</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900">Our advice: use all three</h2>
      <p>
        You don't have to pick one provider. Several providers working together usually do
        better. Use OpenAI for English comments that need detailed categories. Use Azure
        when enterprise compliance requires it. Use Llama Guard for sensitive content that
        must stay on your servers, at no API cost.
        </p>
      <p>
        OpenModeration takes a different route: it runs its own moderation AI and has delicate
        cases cross-checked by other AI models. The engine is model-agnostic, so when a better or
        cheaper model comes out, we plug it in quickly, and nothing changes on your side.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
  </GlossaryAutoLink>

  <BlogArticleExtras />

  <section class="border-t border-surface-100 bg-surface-50 py-12">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-surface-900">Keep exploring</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li><a href="/content-moderation-api" class="font-medium text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-500">One content moderation API for all three providers &rarr;</a></li>
        <li><a href="/alternatives/openai-moderation" class="font-medium text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-500">OpenAI Moderation alternative: the workflow around the scores &rarr;</a></li>
        <li><a href="/alternatives/azure-content-safety" class="font-medium text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-500">Azure Content Safety alternative: no lock-in &rarr;</a></li>
        <li><a href="/features" class="font-medium text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-500">One integration, every provider &rarr;</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

